ck from the  dead we've heard nothing else about the  highly anticipated indie horror game  [Music]  Tech and cross street fighter was  announced all the way back in 2010 for  ps3 and xbox 360 before basically  vanishing producer cut to hero Hirata  assured fans in 2014 even said again in  2015 that it wasn't cancelled but in  April 2016 Hirata revealed that the  crossover fighting game was put on hold  and that publisher Bandai Namco was  waiting for the right time to release it  we just don't know when that time will  be not that we knew much about tech and  cross street fighter in the first place  [Music]  Dead Island 2 was revealed at e3 2014  with a memorable trailer and got a  spring 2015 release window of course it  missed that window and was delayed to  2016 it then lost its former developer  jager in July 2015 but publisher Deep  Silver assured us it wasn't cancelled in  March 2016 we learned that little big  planet 3 developer sumo digital took  over dead island tues development and  that's the last we heard about the  zombie survival sequel so far we know  that Dead Island 2 will have four  playable characters a player co-op in a  sunny California setting  [Music]  battle cry is a mobile like gun free  arena game with its own dedicated  developer in battle cry studios it had a  trailer and even signups for a global  beta in 2015 before dropping off the map  publisher Bethesda expressed concerns  about its quality toward the end of that  year explaining its absence from events  it's been over a year and we haven't  received an update whether positive or  negative yep this is the obligatory half  life 3 mention half life 2 episode 3 was  announced back in two thousand six but  never materialized it also wasn't  cancelled either in a recent reddit AMA  valve boss Gabe Newell said there was  still a possibility of more games in the  half-life portal universe which means  this quintessential missing game is  still floating in limbo we're hoping  2017 holds the